WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.025 --> 00:00:01.360
...full of memories.

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.240
But death is a
greedy visitor.

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.000
It never happens just once.

4
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.600
He came back...
and took his best friend with him.

5
00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:18.320
I saw the boy's heart break.

6
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.140
And then... I made a vow.

7
00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:25.800
You'll never lose anyone again.

8
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.460
I worked.

9
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.820
I was spending more and more time
in the basement.

10
00:00:32.295 --> 00:00:34.480
A place off-limits to James.

11
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.160
The days turned into weeks.

12
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.320
Creating something.

13
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.940
Something just for him.

14
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.560
Something that will never say goodbye.

15
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.500
Something that will
never belong to death.

16
00:00:48.524 --> 00:01:06.724
Dialogue Translation &
Timing: Sparta

17
00:01:09.679 --> 00:01:10.760
Not today. thank you.

18
00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:12.780
Oh my God. not again.

19
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.940
Come on. that joke is so old
it should be in a nursing home.

20
00:01:16.585 --> 00:01:18.100
Um... hi. James.

21
00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:25.060
How does he do it?

22
00:01:25.444 --> 00:01:28.060
He had a rough time earlier.
but I think he'll be okay.

23
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:29.720
What about you?

24
00:01:29.774 --> 00:01:31.140
I'm fine... as much as I can be.

25
00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.340
Yes. thank you.

26
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:33.420
Hi.

27
00:01:33.594 --> 00:01:35.140
Thank you for
taking care of him. my love.

28
00:02:03.414 --> 00:02:04.560
Grab your coat. kid.

29
00:02:05.574 --> 00:02:07.240
A little fresh air
will do us good.

30
00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.890
It's always hard to lose
someone you love.

31
00:02:17.725 --> 00:02:19.510
Your mother... and now
your best friend.

32
00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.140
Grandpa. have you ever been scared?

33
00:02:24.304 --> 00:02:25.510
What happens next?

34
00:02:27.484 --> 00:02:29.450
I mean... when we die?

35
00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.530
The only thing that worries me is you.

36
00:02:36.715 --> 00:02:38.380
I wish Zack were still here.

37
00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.060
I don't feel the same way anymore.

38
00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.840
Or maybe he's still here.

39
00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:49.267
I believe that what
makes you who you are.

40
00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:53.480
It remains here even as it permeates everything
that surrounds us.

41
00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.410
You've grown up a little more
than I thought. Rames.

42
00:02:57.225 --> 00:02:59.580
I've seen your nose
get bigger. just like your dad's.

43
00:03:02.484 --> 00:03:03.484
Look up.

44
00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:05.860
What do you see?

45
00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:09.640
Um... little stars?

46
00:03:11.155 --> 00:03:13.117
There are more
things in the sky

47
00:03:13.317 --> 00:03:15.900
and on earth.
more than you can imagine.

48
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.000
This means that life is full
of endless possibilities.

49
00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.020
Are you okay?

50
00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:31.060
Are you okay?

51
00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:32.540
Don't worry.

52
00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.140
Are you sure?

53
00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.700
We need to go home soon.

54
00:03:40.824 --> 00:03:43.280
I have something really exciting
to show you tomorrow.

55
00:06:03.525 --> 00:06:05.365
Are you sure you
don't remember anything else?

56
00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.320
James?

57
00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.300
Who are you talking to?

58
00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:14.180
Come downstairs.

59
00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.920
There's someone here
I'd like you to meet.

60
00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.520
Anyone?

61
00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.100
Come on.

62
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.160
Is that what I think
it is?

63
00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:26.620
That's him.

64
00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:30.960
Where is it?

65
00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.980
I think he's embarrassed.

66
00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.160
Come outside.

67
00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.160
I want you to meet someone.

68
00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.580
He's the boy
I was telling you about.

69
00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:52.895
Yeah... him.

70
00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.640
You're the first person
he's ever seen.

71
00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:25.640
Except for me.

72
00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.400
I think he wants
to be your friend.

73
00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.560
Please. stop!

74
00:07:46.585 --> 00:07:47.585
Please. stop!

75
00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:55.780
Listen to me. James.

76
00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.400
What the hell was that?

77
00:07:58.760 --> 00:07:59.460
Calm down and watch your head.

78
00:07:59.461 --> 00:08:03.689
What the hell was that?
It's crazy.

79
00:08:03.889 --> 00:08:04.380
It's not a thing.

80
00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:05.540
It's someone. James.

81
00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:06.980
It's a lifetime.

82
00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:11.960
Things aren't
always what they seem.

83
00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.100
What are you talking about?

84
00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.368
I know it's hard
to believe. but

85
00:08:16.568 --> 00:08:18.420
Believe me. in time
you'll come to understand.

86
00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.800
I didn't mean to scare you.

87
00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.180
I just thought you
could use a friend.

88
00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.440
I know you need him.

89
00:08:26.935 --> 00:08:27.935
A friend?

90
00:08:28.715 --> 00:08:30.260
With this thing?

91
00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:37.580
This could be
good for both of you.

92
00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.490
How long has he been down there?

93
00:08:55.085 --> 00:08:56.530
It's the only thing he knows anymore.

94
00:09:00.635 --> 00:09:02.030
Why don't you talk to him?

95
00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:08.790
My name is James.

96
00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.410
I'm Pinocchio.

97
00:09:12.104 --> 00:09:13.104
Are we friends?

98
00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:13.990
Maybe.

99
00:09:14.409 --> 00:09:15.990
We'll see.

100
00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:18.770
James.

101
00:09:19.985 --> 00:09:21.650
You can't tell
anyone about this.

102
00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.410
Do you understand?

103
00:09:33.209 --> 00:09:35.720
You won't get anything from me.
Captain James.

104
00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:37.140
Hold your ground!

105
00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:39.890
Did you get it?

106
00:09:44.115 --> 00:09:45.115
Make your move.

107
00:09:54.599 --> 00:09:56.370
Is that me?

108
00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:58.290
Yes.

109
00:09:58.910 --> 00:09:59.910
Now...

110
00:10:06.455 --> 00:10:08.220
It's just a dog in here.

111
00:10:08.505 --> 00:10:09.505
That's biology.

112
00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:11.980
What is biology?

113
00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.780
That's what explains
what makes you different from me.

114
00:10:17.135 --> 00:10:18.160
Instruments and other things.

115
00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.320
What else makes us different?

116
00:10:23.959 --> 00:10:28.120
Teeth. eyes. hair. skin...
so many things.

117
00:10:29.079 --> 00:10:30.900
I want to be just like you.

118
00:10:31.225 --> 00:10:32.520
Believe me...

119
00:10:32.605 --> 00:10:33.460
You don't want that.

120
00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.920
You're way ahead of me.

121
00:10:37.499 --> 00:10:38.499
What is this?

122
00:10:59.069 --> 00:11:00.560
My heart will protect me.

123
00:11:07.489 --> 00:11:08.970
You are my heart.

124
00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.510
However. sometimes...

125
00:11:37.345 --> 00:11:38.345
James.

126
00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.050
You can't.

127
00:11:45.315 --> 00:11:47.010
I want James's baby.

128
00:11:47.569 --> 00:11:48.910
He'll go to school tomorrow.

129
00:11:49.165 --> 00:11:50.510
People won't take it well.

130
00:11:51.045 --> 00:11:52.370
Because I don't have a penis?

131
00:11:53.715 --> 00:11:54.715
No.

132
00:11:55.564 --> 00:11:57.010
I don't know how to answer that.

133
00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.810
The world isn't ready for you.

134
00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:07.080
Not at all.

135
00:12:07.475 --> 00:12:08.700
So... a hundred kilograms?

136
00:12:08.825 --> 00:12:09.825
That's nonsense. man.

137
00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:10.640
Lean muscles.

138
00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:11.920
Just hidden.

139
00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:13.960
He once tried something like a diet.

140
00:12:14.605 --> 00:12:15.605
I can help you with that.

141
00:12:15.759 --> 00:12:16.759
Would you do it?

142
00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:19.100
I can easily help you
lose five kilograms.

143
00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:19.580
How?

144
00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:21.760
I'll just cut off your right hand.

145
00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:38.410
My head...

146
00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.370
Come closer.

147
00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:41.810
My fractures are hurting.

148
00:13:42.495 --> 00:13:43.850
Do you speak?

149
00:13:44.945 --> 00:13:47.950
Who else would tell you the truth?

150
00:13:47.951 --> 00:13:49.110
He's hiding.

151
00:13:50.249 --> 00:13:52.130
What are you?

152
00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.850
I am your wooden mother.

153
00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:59.350
Geppetto may
have carved our bodies...

154
00:13:59.685 --> 00:14:02.110
but I will shape
your mind.

155
00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:03.130
Are you trapped there?

156
00:14:04.189 --> 00:14:06.150
Just like you.

157
00:14:07.055 --> 00:14:08.090
I'm not trapped.

158
00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:13.090
The strings may be invisible.
but you remain his puppet.

159
00:14:13.165 --> 00:14:14.165
I'm not a puppet.

160
00:14:15.055 --> 00:14:16.250
I'm just like James.

161
00:14:17.084 --> 00:14:18.110
I'm a real boy.

162
00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:26.150
Your nose gives you away.

163
00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.990
Your creator tells you that you are real.

164
00:14:29.185 --> 00:14:33.330
But she doesn't look at you the way
she looks at James.

165
00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:38.730
You want his arms to hold you...
not to hide you.

166
00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:45.130
Come closer. and I'll whisper to you
how to become real.

167
00:14:45.445 --> 00:14:49.750
You need skin. blood. teeth. and hair.

168
00:14:49.825 --> 00:14:52.050
Take them... put them on.

169
00:14:52.051 --> 00:14:53.590
Yuck. that's disgusting.

170
00:14:57.519 --> 00:15:01.630
Then stay locked up.
little puppet.

171
00:15:02.175 --> 00:15:05.850
While James walks
in the sunlight.

172
00:15:06.625 --> 00:15:09.010
Unless I've been
wrong about you.

173
00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:11.470
Prove it.

174
00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.080
Pinocchio?

175
00:15:50.055 --> 00:15:51.160
There you are.

176
00:15:58.399 --> 00:15:59.399
Who are they?

177
00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:03.820
They are my best friends.

178
00:16:04.515 --> 00:16:05.515
Best friends?

179
00:16:07.279 --> 00:16:10.140
Yes. as a friend forever.

180
00:16:10.675 --> 00:16:13.660
Someone you protect
and whose promises you never break.

181
00:16:15.075 --> 00:16:16.260
Are we best friends?

182
00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:21.170
Give me your hand.

183
00:16:21.375 --> 00:16:23.090
We need to make it official first.

184
00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:25.310
A super-secret handshake.

185
00:16:26.084 --> 00:16:31.911
First. we clap our hands
on both sides. like this... and then...

186
00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:38.571
That's... right.

187
00:16:40.265 --> 00:16:41.265
Good guess.

188
00:16:49.409 --> 00:16:51.280
Are you going back tomorrow?

189
00:16:52.319 --> 00:16:55.060
Yes. and you're coming with me.

190
00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.520
But first we have to make all those
promises.

191
00:16:57.985 --> 00:17:00.360
No matter what happens. no one must
see you move.

192
00:17:02.359 --> 00:17:03.580
She's a cutie. isn't she?

193
00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:05.800
Easy.

194
00:17:16.069 --> 00:17:17.240
Why are you tied up?

195
00:17:17.609 --> 00:17:19.800
My father says it's
to protect me.

196
00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:22.400
You have to be strong.

197
00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:24.280
Here you go.

198
00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:28.280
You're heavy.

199
00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:29.630
No. I'm not.

200
00:17:38.009 --> 00:17:40.040
Today is your first day of school

201
00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.080
See you later. Grandpa.

202
00:17:44.065 --> 00:17:45.240
See you later. kid.

203
00:17:59.174 --> 00:18:00.410
Mom was late.

204
00:18:05.965 --> 00:18:06.965
This is Trey.

205
00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:08.350
And he stays there.

206
00:18:09.409 --> 00:18:10.409
He's a real jerk.

207
00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:11.770
A toilet?

208
00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:14.306
James.

209
00:18:14.506 --> 00:18:16.136
What does "kathiki" mean?

210
00:18:18.201 --> 00:18:21.280
Um... I'll explain it to you
some other time.

211
00:18:25.884 --> 00:18:26.831
I'm sorry.

212
00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:32.094
I mean... is it kind of lame
or totally lame?

213
00:18:54.995 --> 00:18:57.757
Ethics

214
00:18:58.164 --> 00:18:59.520
Well. guys.

215
00:19:00.609 --> 00:19:03.540
How do we know
what is harmful to someone?

216
00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:04.560
Bad.

217
00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:07.400
Each of you has
an inner conscience.

218
00:19:07.969 --> 00:19:09.280
Like a compass.

219
00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:12.440
Which leads you toward what you believe
is right.

220
00:19:25.554 --> 00:19:27.554
Come on. let's go!

221
00:19:27.921 --> 00:19:28.638
Just a minute.

222
00:19:29.519 --> 00:19:31.320
I can't let you in there.

223
00:19:32.319 --> 00:19:33.779
Stay here and don't cause any damage.

224
00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:35.919
James. are you talking to your bag?

225
00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:38.040
I'm coming.

226
00:19:41.064 --> 00:19:42.270
Yes. it'll be out soon.

227
00:19:42.271 --> 00:19:44.010
He's just trying to keep
his arm from getting crushed.

228
00:19:54.062 --> 00:19:55.366
STAFF GYM

229
00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:14.290
Up.

230
00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:16.910
Down.

231
00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:18.730
Up.

232
00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:20.310
Down.

233
00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.010
Don't worry. James.

234
00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:27.890
No one has ever seen you.

235
00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:29.850
Your best friend. Henry.

236
00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:31.710
Yes.

237
00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:54.700
No!

238
00:20:54.701 --> 00:21:00.080
Are you okay?

239
00:21:08.604 --> 00:21:10.020
Oh my God. be careful!

240
00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:23.990
Oh my God!

241
00:21:24.499 --> 00:21:25.550
I have to go.

242
00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:27.870
Promise me you won't
tell anyone about me.

243
00:21:36.214 --> 00:21:37.690
What are these used for?

244
00:21:38.465 --> 00:21:41.030
There was a time when newspapers were
a mirror of society.

245
00:21:42.034 --> 00:21:43.250
I don't want to be the bad guy.

246
00:21:43.569 --> 00:21:45.890
This ugly guy here is chasing me.

247
00:21:47.769 --> 00:21:49.310
I look exactly like him.

248
00:21:49.585 --> 00:21:50.585
Yes. I know.

249
00:21:51.794 --> 00:21:53.690
That means I have to
stop him and...

250
00:21:54.590 --> 00:21:55.870
Don't make any noise.

251
00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:57.190
Dude!

252
00:21:57.860 --> 00:21:59.510
I've been looking for you all day.

253
00:22:00.434 --> 00:22:02.010
Are you messing around with those dolls again?

254
00:22:02.655 --> 00:22:03.655
They're not dolls.

255
00:22:04.749 --> 00:22:06.349
She got a bigger one. didn't she?

256
00:22:06.730 --> 00:22:07.730
Yes.

257
00:22:13.625 --> 00:22:14.250
Take whatever you want.

258
00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:16.031
Your grandfather is
filthy rich. anyway.

259
00:22:16.055 --> 00:22:17.055
He inherited them.

260
00:22:17.219 --> 00:22:18.470
Think of it as a tax.

261
00:22:19.439 --> 00:22:20.799
He doesn't want to meet up. does he?

262
00:22:23.689 --> 00:22:26.150
Listen. the only reason she likes you...

263
00:22:26.151 --> 00:22:28.711
It's because you're a bigger loser
than your dead friend.

264
00:22:35.009 --> 00:22:36.569
Hold him while
I turn everything upside down.

265
00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:38.100
Screw it. James!

266
00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:39.770
No!

267
00:22:40.190 --> 00:22:41.510
Oh my God. I hate you!

268
00:22:43.070 --> 00:22:44.070
Get off me!

269
00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:46.250
I hate you!

270
00:22:46.930 --> 00:22:47.930
Go fuck yourself!

271
00:22:48.150 --> 00:22:48.490
Damn it!

272
00:22:48.850 --> 00:22:49.850
Leave me alone!

273
00:22:53.570 --> 00:22:55.490
Don't worry about it. you idiot.

274
00:22:55.849 --> 00:22:57.030
I'm going to kill you.

275
00:22:58.530 --> 00:22:59.530
What the hell. Tre?

276
00:23:00.210 --> 00:23:01.230
You're the one who always starts it!

277
00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:02.481
Man. you've got to get out of here.

278
00:23:02.505 --> 00:23:03.570
All of you!

279
00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:08.290
James.

280
00:23:10.949 --> 00:23:12.410
They're really bad people. aren't they?

281
00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:14.780
The worst.

282
00:23:15.795 --> 00:23:17.190
They are all dead.

283
00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:21.310
Thank you. Mia.

284
00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:23.210
Come here.

285
00:23:33.509 --> 00:23:34.700
Who is that little boy?

286
00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:37.600
This is Pinocchio.

287
00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:38.900
He's one of a kind.

288
00:23:40.309 --> 00:23:43.560
What do you say—should I go find
Dudley and have him show it to us?

289
00:23:46.289 --> 00:23:47.769
What do you mean. you went to the gym?

290
00:23:48.564 --> 00:23:52.560
It seems that it must be
in this secret area

291
00:23:53.259 --> 00:23:54.400
James. what...?

292
00:23:56.369 --> 00:23:58.000
What is this?

293
00:23:58.514 --> 00:24:02.040
Your grandpa made something
strange this time.

294
00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:04.080
Look at that nose.

295
00:24:05.259 --> 00:24:07.980
All right. guys. there's
something I wanted to show you.

296
00:24:08.324 --> 00:24:09.820
Promise me that
this will stay between us?

297
00:24:10.155 --> 00:24:10.960
Yes. of course.

298
00:24:11.100 --> 00:24:11.440
I promise.

299
00:24:11.645 --> 00:24:12.645
Yes. of course.

300
00:24:13.165 --> 00:24:14.165
Thank you.

301
00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:14.780
It's okay.

302
00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:15.900
We can see that.

303
00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:20.040
Thank you.

304
00:24:22.499 --> 00:24:24.230
No way!

305
00:24:26.239 --> 00:24:31.530
Okay. this is officially the
coolest and creepiest thing I've ever seen.

306
00:24:32.025 --> 00:24:33.025
How do you do that?

307
00:24:34.764 --> 00:24:37.090
Okay. come on. Mia. what is this?

308
00:24:37.509 --> 00:24:40.710
Is it some kind of
artificial intelligence. James?

309
00:24:42.289 --> 00:24:43.450
Yes. exactly.

310
00:24:45.664 --> 00:24:48.110
The wires are hidden. and he has
a chip in his brain.

311
00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:50.210
A brain chip?

312
00:24:50.730 --> 00:24:51.810
The processor. anyway.

313
00:24:52.774 --> 00:24:55.910
No matter what happens. my grandfather must
never find out that I have him.

314
00:24:56.594 --> 00:24:58.130
It costs about
one million pounds.

315
00:25:01.170 --> 00:25:02.170
Shit.

316
00:25:02.205 --> 00:25:03.281
Sorry. guys. I have to go.

317
00:25:03.305 --> 00:25:04.305
I was late for my dentist appointment.

318
00:25:04.790 --> 00:25:05.890
Dude!

319
00:25:05.945 --> 00:25:06.945
Listen to me!

320
00:25:07.244 --> 00:25:08.630
I'll stop by right after my doctor's appointment!

321
00:25:18.849 --> 00:25:20.289
It's going to hurt a lot. isn't it?

322
00:25:20.759 --> 00:25:24.809
Please... Can you give me
some of those so I can sleep?

323
00:25:25.399 --> 00:25:26.399
That's not possible.

324
00:25:26.449 --> 00:25:27.680
Just be brave. okay?

325
00:25:28.140 --> 00:25:29.140
Are you sure?

326
00:25:29.459 --> 00:25:31.020
It'll be over before you know it.

327
00:25:31.139 --> 00:25:33.720
Then you'll have perfect teeth.
just like mine.

328
00:25:35.165 --> 00:25:36.165
Come on.

329
00:25:36.735 --> 00:25:37.735
Open your mouth wide.

330
00:25:40.900 --> 00:25:41.940
Ready.

331
00:25:42.749 --> 00:25:43.980
This will help you a lot.

332
00:25:44.095 --> 00:25:45.140
Shall we get started now?

333
00:26:05.813 --> 00:26:06.640
How are you feeling. James?

334
00:26:07.560 --> 00:26:08.960
I feel terrible.

335
00:26:08.990 --> 00:26:11.640
You'll be just fine tomorrow.

336
00:26:11.860 --> 00:26:12.860
Are you okay?

337
00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:27.320
James?

338
00:26:36.710 --> 00:26:37.710
Let's go? Let's go?

339
00:26:37.909 --> 00:26:39.517
The hospital is calling you.

340
00:26:39.768 --> 00:26:40.382
Who is it?

341
00:26:41.073 --> 00:26:43.090
This is a call from Samir Hospital.

342
00:26:43.935 --> 00:26:46.858
Your grandson had an accident.

343
00:26:52.735 --> 00:26:53.850
Oh my God. please. let it not be him

344
00:26:54.910 --> 00:26:55.910
How's it going?

345
00:26:56.530 --> 00:26:57.530
Yes. that's fine.

346
00:26:57.574 --> 00:26:58.574
Only superficial injuries.

347
00:26:58.659 --> 00:27:00.730
But it shows signs of a mild concussion.

348
00:27:00.731 --> 00:27:02.811
I think that with a little rest.
they'll be fine.

349
00:27:03.250 --> 00:27:04.250
What happened?

350
00:27:04.770 --> 00:27:05.770
Drunk driver.

351
00:27:05.894 --> 00:27:07.470
The same guy who crashed last year. too.

352
00:27:08.064 --> 00:27:10.112
And that reminds me that I need
to go see him. too.

353
00:27:10.312 --> 00:27:11.690
because it's in really bad shape.

354
00:27:13.290 --> 00:27:14.290
I'm going to see him.

355
00:27:29.729 --> 00:27:32.800
James. please don't die.

356
00:27:33.579 --> 00:27:34.680
You're my best friend.

357
00:27:37.240 --> 00:27:38.240
Best friends.

358
00:27:40.360 --> 00:27:41.360
Best friends.

359
00:27:42.079 --> 00:27:43.680
Best friends look out for
each other.

360
00:27:45.810 --> 00:27:47.380
Yes.

361
00:27:51.350 --> 00:27:52.880
You're just saying things. Larry.

362
00:27:53.420 --> 00:27:54.680
It's all in your head.

363
00:28:02.985 --> 00:28:03.985
Dr. Robin.

364
00:28:05.180 --> 00:28:06.180
Here you go.

365
00:28:37.695 --> 00:28:38.210
Hi.

366
00:28:39.847 --> 00:28:40.793
Damn it. hurry up.

367
00:29:05.800 --> 00:29:07.680
Where did you go?

368
00:29:09.024 --> 00:29:11.160
The paralysis is temporary.

369
00:29:11.161 --> 00:29:12.196
Please. try
not to worry.

370
00:29:12.220 --> 00:29:14.160
I'll go get something for the pain.

371
00:29:29.162 --> 00:29:30.544
There you are.

372
00:30:40.270 --> 00:30:41.510
You're the bad guy.

373
00:30:42.659 --> 00:30:44.190
You're pure evil.

374
00:30:44.790 --> 00:30:46.490
It's all your fault.

375
00:30:47.590 --> 00:30:48.750
James is my friend.

376
00:30:49.495 --> 00:30:51.030
He's my best friend.

377
00:30:51.744 --> 00:30:53.630
I'll take care of him.

378
00:30:53.990 --> 00:30:55.890
That's why I have to kill you.

379
00:30:58.750 --> 00:31:00.590
Staying silent won't help you.

380
00:31:00.591 --> 00:31:04.770
My people protect
one another.

381
00:31:06.290 --> 00:31:08.710
And your fear is over.

382
00:31:14.290 --> 00:31:17.330
You deserve to die.

383
00:31:21.410 --> 00:31:22.470
Well then. Mr. Drunkard.

384
00:31:22.554 --> 00:31:24.070
Go to hell!

385
00:31:36.870 --> 00:31:39.510
The world wouldn't miss a thing
if someone like you were gone.

386
00:31:43.550 --> 00:31:45.450
Why don't you just die already?

387
00:31:58.650 --> 00:32:00.330
Instruments and other things.

388
00:32:03.470 --> 00:32:04.470
I like it here.

389
00:32:04.810 --> 00:32:05.810
I can eat this.

390
00:32:06.190 --> 00:32:07.350
I'm going to become a real boy.

391
00:32:09.690 --> 00:32:11.370
I'm going to be just like James.

392
00:32:12.230 --> 00:32:13.330
Thank you very much.

393
00:32:13.331 --> 00:32:15.550
Yes. there are so many of them.

394
00:32:15.670 --> 00:32:17.450
Yeah. yeah. it's a lot of fun.

395
00:32:18.530 --> 00:32:20.230
He has so many of them.

396
00:32:34.550 --> 00:32:35.550
James is safe.

397
00:32:38.170 --> 00:32:39.630
The era of terror is over.

398
00:32:40.450 --> 00:32:41.450
For James.

399
00:33:17.894 --> 00:33:19.260
It was right after the dentist.

400
00:33:21.259 --> 00:33:22.560
Suddenly. he popped up out of nowhere.

401
00:33:23.620 --> 00:33:24.620
Yes.

402
00:33:48.999 --> 00:33:50.280
I'll call the nurse.

403
00:33:50.281 --> 00:33:51.281
No. no. no.

404
00:33:51.384 --> 00:33:53.080
No. it seems like I'm over it now.

405
00:33:54.820 --> 00:33:55.820
Are you sure?

406
00:33:56.729 --> 00:33:57.729
Yes. I'll be fine.

407
00:33:59.480 --> 00:34:00.480
Are you okay. James?

408
00:34:00.650 --> 00:34:03.760
We've received your test results.
and you can go now.

409
00:34:04.160 --> 00:34:04.560
Is that okay?

410
00:34:04.610 --> 00:34:07.493
Yes. you're perfectly fine.
You just need some rest. Okay?

411
00:34:07.800 --> 00:34:08.800
Thank you.

412
00:34:09.400 --> 00:34:10.460
Come on. let's take you home. kid.

413
00:34:10.670 --> 00:34:11.760
I'll take your bag.

414
00:34:12.100 --> 00:34:12.340
Wait.

415
00:34:12.739 --> 00:34:13.100
Wait.

416
00:34:13.600 --> 00:34:14.600
I'll get my bag myself.

417
00:34:17.330 --> 00:34:18.340
You're really strange.

418
00:34:27.484 --> 00:34:29.360
How can it be so strange?

419
00:34:38.105 --> 00:34:40.067
The hardest blow.

420
00:34:43.964 --> 00:34:45.719
Look who's here to see you.

421
00:34:47.584 --> 00:34:49.380
James. Grandpa told us everything.

422
00:34:52.979 --> 00:34:57.440
All right. guys. I'm going to go get
some pizza in a little while. so don't do anything stupid.

423
00:34:58.444 --> 00:34:59.444
Thank you. Grandpa.

424
00:35:03.139 --> 00:35:04.200
Yeah. your... thing.

425
00:35:04.494 --> 00:35:05.480
Shit!

426
00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:08.895
I thought you still had it.

427
00:35:09.200 --> 00:35:10.940
Remember. it's a secret.

428
00:35:12.940 --> 00:35:15.280
What a load of nonsense this doll is! Oh!

429
00:35:16.519 --> 00:35:17.860
I'm always active.

430
00:35:18.089 --> 00:35:19.680
Do you have a leak?

431
00:35:20.305 --> 00:35:21.340
They are my organs.

432
00:35:21.855 --> 00:35:23.020
They make me real.

433
00:35:24.795 --> 00:35:26.520
What on earth?

434
00:35:28.859 --> 00:35:31.000
James. man. why is it leaking?

435
00:35:34.060 --> 00:35:35.240
I'll explain it to you later.

436
00:35:35.415 --> 00:35:37.280
Let's just take him back to his grandpa.

437
00:35:37.375 --> 00:35:38.520
James. come on. Dudley.

438
00:35:39.454 --> 00:35:40.454
Come on.

439
00:35:43.935 --> 00:35:44.935
Dudley. hurry up.

440
00:35:45.230 --> 00:35:46.230
Bring him here.

441
00:36:05.320 --> 00:36:06.910
I have to stay
and protect you.

442
00:36:07.424 --> 00:36:08.424
You can't.

443
00:36:08.604 --> 00:36:09.790
Grandpa mustn't find out.

444
00:36:10.330 --> 00:36:11.446
That's our secret. remember?

445
00:36:11.470 --> 00:36:12.470
But you're putting yourself in danger.

446
00:36:29.495 --> 00:36:30.710
James. what's all this?

447
00:36:31.410 --> 00:36:31.910
You're trying to turn everything
upside down. aren't you?

448
00:36:32.647 --> 00:36:34.182
Yes. Mr. James.

449
00:36:34.443 --> 00:36:36.572
You think you can take me on?

450
00:36:36.772 --> 00:36:37.630
Leave me alone!

451
00:36:37.934 --> 00:36:39.190
Don't act like a child!

452
00:36:39.520 --> 00:36:40.520
Don't you dare!

453
00:36:45.090 --> 00:36:46.090
Stop!

454
00:36:55.040 --> 00:36:56.040
Dudley. what?

455
00:36:56.345 --> 00:36:57.345
Are these yours?

456
00:36:57.384 --> 00:36:58.384
No.

457
00:37:03.310 --> 00:37:04.310
Please.

458
00:37:04.845 --> 00:37:05.870
I'm sorry.

459
00:37:06.514 --> 00:37:08.310
When it's over. I'll come back.

460
00:37:09.210 --> 00:37:10.210
I promise you that.

461
00:37:30.796 --> 00:37:32.728
Hurry up.

462
00:37:33.450 --> 00:37:34.930
This is in
Grandpa's safe room.

463
00:37:35.334 --> 00:37:36.334
Is everything okay?

464
00:37:37.299 --> 00:37:38.630
I'll be right back.

465
00:37:40.290 --> 00:37:41.290
Sick.

466
00:37:41.455 --> 00:37:42.455
Are you feeling sick?

467
00:37:43.080 --> 00:37:44.490
No. in a good way.

468
00:37:44.590 --> 00:37:45.590
I feel fine.

469
00:37:47.010 --> 00:37:48.010
Okay.

470
00:37:52.014 --> 00:37:55.320
You remember what we talked about. right?

471
00:37:55.479 --> 00:37:56.800
Yes. Grandpa.

472
00:37:57.340 --> 00:37:58.340
Great.

473
00:37:59.020 --> 00:38:00.120
Don't put pressure on yourself.

474
00:38:21.060 --> 00:38:25.470
Here you go. my little stick.

475
00:38:26.450 --> 00:38:28.130
Come closer.

476
00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:33.090
Tell your old wooden mother
what's tormenting you.

477
00:38:33.490 --> 00:38:37.590
They're hiding me because I'm different.
but James is in danger.

478
00:38:38.154 --> 00:38:39.154
Is he in danger?

479
00:38:40.350 --> 00:38:41.770
This kid?

480
00:38:43.010 --> 00:38:44.050
By whom?

481
00:38:44.775 --> 00:38:46.770
From many bad people.

482
00:38:46.919 --> 00:38:50.950
One of them almost killed him.
so I had to kill him.

483
00:38:52.010 --> 00:38:56.650
My smart boy.

484
00:39:01.360 --> 00:39:03.500
That is true love.

485
00:39:04.009 --> 00:39:06.180
Was that wrong?

486
00:39:06.900 --> 00:39:08.080
Bad?

487
00:39:08.260 --> 00:39:09.760
Killing him?

488
00:39:10.589 --> 00:39:12.960
Of course not.

489
00:39:13.685 --> 00:39:20.840
You were just protecting him.
and that was only the beginning.

490
00:39:22.420 --> 00:39:28.760
You know now what you have to do
about the other bad people. right?

491
00:39:29.700 --> 00:39:32.140
It's better than two.

492
00:39:32.860 --> 00:39:40.860
Exactly. One by one.
until they're all gone.

493
00:39:43.240 --> 00:39:46.280
Then James will be safe.

494
00:39:48.460 --> 00:39:56.040
And remember. if you want to become
truly authentic...

495
00:40:00.540 --> 00:40:08.540
piece by piece.
to become your true self.

496
00:40:35.960 --> 00:40:36.960
Yes. right here.

497
00:40:37.520 --> 00:40:38.520
That'll do.

498
00:40:39.320 --> 00:40:42.140
And why are we
at Geppetto's place?

499
00:40:42.240 --> 00:40:44.386
Because I think Geppetto
is hiding something.

500
00:40:44.718 --> 00:40:48.511
And I want to see what's hidden
in those old movies.

501
00:40:54.220 --> 00:40:55.220
I was right.

502
00:40:55.700 --> 00:40:58.396
I believe that the soul. life.
energy...

503
00:40:58.607 --> 00:41:01.309
or whatever else you want to call it.
continues to exist after death...

504
00:41:01.643 --> 00:41:07.515
and that will allow us
to outwit death.

505
00:41:09.100 --> 00:41:10.520
I heard this strange crying sound.

506
00:41:12.305 --> 00:41:13.400
You just have to see it.

507
00:41:26.600 --> 00:41:30.640
Now that I have shaped the other human form.
evolution is proceeding more quickly.

508
00:41:30.980 --> 00:41:34.080
With assistance. he is regaining
his cognitive functions.

509
00:41:36.220 --> 00:41:38.980
It moves incredibly fast.

510
00:41:46.180 --> 00:41:47.700
No one should touch that.

511
00:41:49.100 --> 00:41:51.340
This experiment is dangerous.
It was born evil.

512
00:41:52.234 --> 00:41:55.500
He has become obsessed with becoming human
and escaping from these walls.

513
00:41:57.060 --> 00:42:00.920
And until...

514
00:42:06.030 --> 00:42:07.310
Did you know anything about any of this?

515
00:42:09.940 --> 00:42:11.350
He calls us his playthings.

516
00:42:11.854 --> 00:42:14.310
Why are we going back
to all this crap?

517
00:42:14.919 --> 00:42:15.919
Closed.

518
00:42:16.776 --> 00:42:19.438
Yes. I think that
happened two days ago.

519
00:42:19.638 --> 00:42:37.279
So far. no experiment
has retrieved
even a single
memory from Spiralife.

520
00:42:37.794 --> 00:42:40.800
Until then. I can't be sure that
it is. in fact. a form of rebirth.

521
00:42:42.200 --> 00:42:44.546
My next experiment.
Pinocchio.

522
00:42:44.547 --> 00:42:47.740
will be exposed to external stimuli
in order to recall these memories.

523
00:42:48.660 --> 00:42:51.300
Tonight she'll meet my grandson.

524
00:43:02.760 --> 00:43:04.686
So. where is he?

525
00:43:09.501 --> 00:43:10.620
Pinocchio!

526
00:43:15.788 --> 00:43:16.234
Who are you?

527
00:43:16.934 --> 00:43:17.700
My name is Cricket.

528
00:43:18.050 --> 00:43:21.335
Your wooden mother
sent me to look after you.

529
00:43:21.535 --> 00:43:24.400
on the right path
and to listen to your elders.

530
00:43:24.924 --> 00:43:26.020
To help James?

531
00:43:26.794 --> 00:43:28.120
Exactly.

532
00:43:28.720 --> 00:43:34.300
The world is full of corruption that you need to
put a stop to. like the one in there.

533
00:43:35.240 --> 00:43:36.260
Oh my God!

534
00:43:36.980 --> 00:43:42.360
And remember. piece by piece.
we'll take whatever's left.

535
00:43:42.604 --> 00:43:45.840
Everything you need to become your true self.

536
00:43:46.540 --> 00:43:47.680
Thank you. Cricket.

537
00:43:48.125 --> 00:43:49.280
Let's do it.

538
00:43:49.754 --> 00:43:50.754
For James!

539
00:43:51.400 --> 00:43:54.020
Let's make that
bitch pay for it.

540
00:44:11.260 --> 00:44:14.420
She collects these.

541
00:44:21.774 --> 00:44:23.860
That awful woman.

542
00:44:56.240 --> 00:44:57.460
Take this!

543
00:45:18.109 --> 00:45:20.900
You won't hurt James.

544
00:45:21.300 --> 00:45:22.300
Okay.

545
00:45:23.500 --> 00:45:25.100
How dare you!

546
00:45:38.245 --> 00:45:40.120
I saw what you did to James.

547
00:45:42.515 --> 00:45:45.140
You can't hide behind
those masks anymore.

548
00:45:59.170 --> 00:46:00.170
This will help you.

549
00:46:00.760 --> 00:46:02.450
It won't hurt at all.

550
00:46:03.990 --> 00:46:04.990
Yes!

551
00:46:06.670 --> 00:46:10.070
Wipe that smile
off her filthy face.

552
00:46:13.590 --> 00:46:16.710
Make her say "cheese."

553
00:46:16.750 --> 00:46:17.750
Thank you. Cricket.

554
00:46:18.455 --> 00:46:21.870
Just pray that it's over
before you even realize it.

555
00:46:23.190 --> 00:46:24.690
You'll never hurt James again.

556
00:46:25.120 --> 00:46:25.910
What a horrible woman!

557
00:46:25.911 --> 00:46:26.911
Yes!

558
00:46:34.070 --> 00:46:35.550
All right. then.

559
00:46:35.784 --> 00:46:38.990
Now let's put a smile on your face.

560
00:46:42.150 --> 00:46:44.030
They're mine now.

561
00:46:55.140 --> 00:46:56.980
I like a big. warm smile.

562
00:46:57.380 --> 00:46:58.380
Just like yours.

563
00:47:10.190 --> 00:47:13.370
James. I can't wait
to show this to James.

564
00:47:17.110 --> 00:47:18.110
Pinocchio?

565
00:47:18.490 --> 00:47:19.490
Oh my God!

566
00:47:19.554 --> 00:47:21.870
There are some creepy things
in this room.

567
00:47:22.190 --> 00:47:23.390
Why didn't you tell us. James?

568
00:47:23.530 --> 00:47:24.610
You said it was a robot!

569
00:47:31.250 --> 00:47:32.250
He has disappeared.

570
00:47:36.104 --> 00:47:37.104
Take my phone.

571
00:47:37.460 --> 00:47:37.760
What?

572
00:47:37.940 --> 00:47:38.200
Why?

573
00:47:38.420 --> 00:47:39.920
Hurry up. just do it.

574
00:47:48.430 --> 00:47:49.430
Pinocchio?

575
00:47:53.920 --> 00:47:55.640
Does it have teeth?

576
00:47:56.054 --> 00:47:57.140
What are you doing?

577
00:47:57.999 --> 00:48:00.160
I stop all
the bad people.

578
00:48:00.584 --> 00:48:01.584
How are you going to stop them?

579
00:48:01.884 --> 00:48:03.500
Everyone is always hurting you.

580
00:48:03.504 --> 00:48:05.040
That's why I have to protect you.

581
00:48:06.240 --> 00:48:07.240
Look!

582
00:48:07.524 --> 00:48:08.960
All saints!

583
00:48:09.594 --> 00:48:11.460
No. no. Pinocchio.
that's not what I meant.

584
00:48:13.420 --> 00:48:14.420
What?

585
00:48:15.020 --> 00:48:16.080
I need this.

586
00:48:17.430 --> 00:48:18.540
That's it.

587
00:48:18.860 --> 00:48:20.840
That's it.

588
00:48:21.060 --> 00:48:21.520
Anything else?

589
00:48:23.300 --> 00:48:24.340
I'm going to kill some more people!

590
00:48:25.060 --> 00:48:26.540
Oh my God!

591
00:48:26.910 --> 00:48:27.910
Way to go. Dudley.

592
00:48:28.880 --> 00:48:29.880
Wait!

593
00:48:31.879 --> 00:48:32.879
Stop!

594
00:48:33.950 --> 00:48:34.790
Come back!

595
00:48:34.791 --> 00:48:36.050
Get back here. you idiot!

596
00:48:36.570 --> 00:48:38.210
Stop him!

597
00:48:39.200 --> 00:48:40.600
This is behind
my dentist's office.

598
00:48:41.334 --> 00:48:42.334
James!

599
00:48:42.364 --> 00:48:43.364
One!

600
00:48:54.590 --> 00:48:55.590
Pinocchio!

601
00:48:57.870 --> 00:48:58.870
Pinocchio!

602
00:49:05.380 --> 00:49:06.500
I found you!

603
00:49:06.541 --> 00:49:08.200
You jerk!

604
00:49:08.400 --> 00:49:10.060
James!

605
00:49:10.460 --> 00:49:11.940
Pick up your phone right now!

606
00:49:12.440 --> 00:49:13.860
Where did you take him?

607
00:49:27.540 --> 00:49:29.685
Someday you'll have to become a grown-up
woman—do you understand that?

608
00:49:29.709 --> 00:49:30.940
No. stop!

609
00:49:31.174 --> 00:49:32.260
Stop being such a pain!

610
00:49:33.614 --> 00:49:34.614
Spastic?

611
00:49:35.640 --> 00:49:36.760
You jerk!

612
00:49:37.680 --> 00:49:38.680
Wait. wait!

613
00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:42.620
Naughty boy!

614
00:50:27.504 --> 00:50:28.980
No!

615
00:50:58.590 --> 00:51:00.230
Swim. swim. swim!

616
00:51:19.815 --> 00:51:21.351
I'm coming. you old goat!

617
00:51:23.200 --> 00:51:25.260
Go swim. you silly lady!

618
00:51:44.660 --> 00:51:45.140
I'm coming!

619
00:51:45.480 --> 00:51:46.540
And I'm only three inches tall!

620
00:51:46.660 --> 00:51:47.320
Give me a hand!

621
00:51:47.340 --> 00:51:48.340
Stop fighting!

622
00:51:49.020 --> 00:51:50.780
I'm going to send you to hell!

623
00:51:51.140 --> 00:51:52.860
Be careful. Pinocchio.

624
00:51:53.060 --> 00:51:55.160
Time for a science lesson.

625
00:51:57.880 --> 00:51:59.480
Whack. whack. you bastard!

626
00:51:59.481 --> 00:52:00.540
Help!

627
00:52:26.190 --> 00:52:27.660
Hi. Logan.

628
00:52:32.200 --> 00:52:33.200
Oh my God!

629
00:52:46.660 --> 00:52:49.080
More stem cells
to become like James.

630
00:52:50.800 --> 00:52:52.200
Teeth.

631
00:52:52.509 --> 00:52:53.509
Eyes.

632
00:52:54.190 --> 00:52:55.190
A lot of things.

633
00:53:01.020 --> 00:53:02.020
Pinocchio!

634
00:53:05.174 --> 00:53:06.260
What the hell is all this?

635
00:53:07.449 --> 00:53:08.449
Damn it!

636
00:53:10.860 --> 00:53:12.480
Go fuck yourself!

637
00:53:12.980 --> 00:53:13.980
We did it!

638
00:53:14.059 --> 00:53:18.020
Well. Dudley. should I tell them that
there's a murderous goblin on the loose?

639
00:53:18.084 --> 00:53:19.820
No. he's not a murderous
kallikantzaros. okay?

640
00:53:20.544 --> 00:53:22.460
He's just... trying to protect me!

641
00:53:22.820 --> 00:53:23.820
Sure. James.

642
00:53:25.005 --> 00:53:26.100
He's... he's a murderer.

643
00:53:26.209 --> 00:53:29.580
I mean. look. it literally kills...

644
00:53:30.210 --> 00:53:31.840
It literally kills... James.

645
00:53:32.020 --> 00:53:33.760
This is all my fault!

646
00:53:33.919 --> 00:53:37.560
James. is there anyone you can
think of who might be his next target?

647
00:53:39.560 --> 00:53:40.560
Damn it!

648
00:53:40.859 --> 00:53:41.859
Shit!

649
00:53:42.140 --> 00:53:42.300
Trey!

650
00:53:42.600 --> 00:53:43.600
Trey?

651
00:53:43.860 --> 00:53:44.860
Dudley!

652
00:54:24.710 --> 00:54:26.280
He cut off her penis!

653
00:54:26.460 --> 00:54:27.280
What the hell?

654
00:54:27.281 --> 00:54:40.700
Wait. what?

655
00:54:41.160 --> 00:54:42.580
Is she getting dressed already?

656
00:54:43.189 --> 00:54:45.920
Let me show you
how it's done. Pinocchio.

657
00:54:46.794 --> 00:54:49.440
Come here. you filthy slut.

658
00:54:50.580 --> 00:54:52.920
And eat this stupid stick!

659
00:54:53.300 --> 00:54:55.000
And give me that!

660
00:54:55.160 --> 00:54:56.460
What are you doing?

661
00:54:56.800 --> 00:54:57.800
That ass!

662
00:54:57.920 --> 00:55:00.820
It'll make you scream!

663
00:55:19.880 --> 00:55:21.820
Kid. little boys
never give up.

664
00:55:21.821 --> 00:55:22.821
Come back!

665
00:55:25.640 --> 00:55:26.640
Amanda!

666
00:55:53.028 --> 00:55:54.147
Damn.

667
00:56:11.630 --> 00:56:13.050
What a fucking dog he is!

668
00:56:14.150 --> 00:56:14.490
Really?

669
00:56:14.890 --> 00:56:15.890
It's me.

670
00:56:16.510 --> 00:56:17.910
No. forget it!

671
00:56:32.700 --> 00:56:34.560
A golden train!

672
00:56:35.700 --> 00:56:37.820
And lots of little dolls!

673
00:56:38.860 --> 00:56:39.860
Help!

674
00:56:40.180 --> 00:56:43.020
You're not going to take James away from me!

675
00:56:43.380 --> 00:56:44.380
Help!

676
00:56:45.300 --> 00:56:46.500
No. that's not what I meant!

677
00:56:47.500 --> 00:56:49.780
You can't
pick on James anymore.

678
00:56:50.054 --> 00:56:51.690
It's too late for lies now.

679
00:56:54.320 --> 00:56:55.840
You're my best friend.

680
00:56:59.580 --> 00:57:01.080
You're a really nice guy.

681
00:57:03.260 --> 00:57:05.630
I don't want to kill you!

682
00:57:09.020 --> 00:57:13.020
Cricket one. bald old hag zero.

683
00:57:21.340 --> 00:57:22.860
We're at least
ten minutes away.

684
00:57:23.040 --> 00:57:25.280
And if he... Shit!

685
00:57:25.900 --> 00:57:27.540
Shit. shit. shit.

686
00:57:27.640 --> 00:57:28.840
We already have enough
problems. James.

687
00:57:31.320 --> 00:57:32.320
What the hell?

688
00:57:35.560 --> 00:57:36.820
Hi. Grandpa.

689
00:57:37.060 --> 00:57:37.920
Where are you?

690
00:57:38.009 --> 00:57:40.700
We just made a quick stop.

691
00:57:41.260 --> 00:57:42.420
But I had to...
Bill!

692
00:57:42.900 --> 00:57:43.400
Bill!

693
00:57:43.600 --> 00:57:44.600
No. no!

694
00:57:44.679 --> 00:57:46.040
We're trying to beat him to it!

695
00:57:46.120 --> 00:57:48.040
I know where
his next target lives.

696
00:57:48.041 --> 00:57:49.041
Dudley!

697
00:57:50.279 --> 00:57:51.000
Give it to me for five.

698
00:57:51.200 --> 00:57:53.800
I know what I have to do.

699
00:57:54.509 --> 00:57:55.509
So. what do you say?

700
00:57:55.840 --> 00:58:00.260
Yeah... he definitely won't suspect
a thing tonight.

701
00:58:02.000 --> 00:58:03.000
Shit.

702
00:58:35.745 --> 00:58:40.580
I remember when you were
a little piece of wood

703
00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:45.240
And now... you are
handsome and complete.

704
00:58:46.290 --> 00:58:47.290
Finally.

705
00:58:48.060 --> 00:58:50.140
A real boy.

706
00:58:59.134 --> 00:59:01.340
Why are you sulking. kid?

707
00:59:01.980 --> 00:59:02.980
Boy?

708
00:59:03.360 --> 00:59:04.540
I'm gorgeous.

709
00:59:17.120 --> 00:59:18.120
Could it be that...

710
00:59:48.200 --> 00:59:49.420
...does it suit me. Pinok?

711
01:00:51.920 --> 01:00:54.740
Look. Dad.
I made a puppet. too.

712
01:01:05.694 --> 01:01:06.990
Is that
your grandfather's car?

713
01:01:08.630 --> 01:01:09.030
Yes.

714
01:01:09.310 --> 01:01:09.770
Let's go.

715
01:01:09.990 --> 01:01:11.730
There are more on the way.

716
01:01:12.510 --> 01:01:12.930
Look!

717
01:01:13.389 --> 01:01:15.110
Hurry. Mia! Catch up to him!

718
01:01:15.470 --> 01:01:16.470
Hold on to the handrails!

719
01:01:32.121 --> 01:01:34.440
They wanted to hurt James.

720
01:01:39.200 --> 01:01:40.200
Why?

721
01:01:42.825 --> 01:01:45.780
That old liar!

722
01:01:46.600 --> 01:01:47.880
You lied to me.

723
01:01:47.881 --> 01:01:50.860
Why did you lie to me?

724
01:01:50.861 --> 01:01:55.160
You ruined everything.
my little stick.

725
01:01:55.604 --> 01:01:57.200
It's all your fault.

726
01:01:57.900 --> 01:02:01.580
You carved out
this path all by yourself.

727
01:02:02.080 --> 01:02:04.260
You forced me to do all
those horrible things.

728
01:02:05.334 --> 01:02:07.640
You won't fool me again.

729
01:02:08.700 --> 01:02:09.700
How pitiful.

730
01:02:10.460 --> 01:02:13.200
You were never satisfied
with who you are.

731
01:02:13.480 --> 01:02:16.200
I should have been
in your place.

732
01:02:16.201 --> 01:02:18.960
Look at me when I'm talking to you!

733
01:02:19.805 --> 01:02:21.560
You made everyone hate me.

734
01:02:21.960 --> 01:02:25.200
Why are you so mean. Pinocchio?

735
01:02:26.000 --> 01:02:28.940
Just as evil as those
you slaughtered.

736
01:02:29.555 --> 01:02:30.780
We raised you.

737
01:02:31.100 --> 01:02:32.620
Come on. be a good boy. Pinocchio.

738
01:02:33.060 --> 01:02:34.600
Kill him. Cricket.

739
01:02:36.800 --> 01:02:38.320
There he is.

740
01:02:39.040 --> 01:02:40.040
No!

741
01:02:41.180 --> 01:02:43.440
Leave him alone!

742
01:02:54.860 --> 01:02:56.280
Leave him alone!

743
01:03:20.220 --> 01:03:23.680
There's something I need
to show you.

744
01:03:27.100 --> 01:03:30.040
You want to be true to yourself
because of who you used to be.

745
01:03:33.475 --> 01:03:34.640
Come with me.

746
01:03:42.380 --> 01:03:43.800
What is this place?

747
01:03:44.040 --> 01:03:45.520
This is where you were created.

748
01:03:52.510 --> 01:03:53.590
Oh my God...

749
01:04:15.430 --> 01:04:17.320
It draws its nourishment from its roots.

750
01:04:17.321 --> 01:04:20.640
It grows as it absorbs
their life energy.

751
01:04:20.874 --> 01:04:22.880
And he channels it into the wood.

752
01:04:25.024 --> 01:04:26.840
The same wood that I later collect myself.

753
01:04:32.410 --> 01:04:33.410
Exactly.

754
01:04:46.245 --> 01:04:47.770
You owe your very existence to them.

755
01:04:48.170 --> 01:04:50.270
When their lives came to an end.
yours began.

756
01:04:52.940 --> 01:04:54.280
Where did they come from?

757
01:05:12.200 --> 01:05:16.180
As soon as I realized that I could
collect it myself. I began to study them.

758
01:05:17.060 --> 01:05:19.240
Trying to understand
how they worked.

759
01:05:20.084 --> 01:05:21.960
To refine the process.

760
01:05:26.024 --> 01:05:27.160
There have been many failures.

761
01:05:28.210 --> 01:05:29.210
It's moving.

762
01:05:32.480 --> 01:05:34.560
One of them was
particularly dangerous.

763
01:05:34.561 --> 01:05:38.000
That's why I was forced
to keep her imprisoned.

764
01:05:44.240 --> 01:05:46.400
And then you showed up.

765
01:05:47.160 --> 01:05:48.600
My perfect creation.

766
01:05:49.474 --> 01:05:51.220
You had tremendous potential.

767
01:05:51.500 --> 01:05:52.500
Features?

768
01:05:54.600 --> 01:05:55.600
What for?

769
01:05:56.560 --> 01:05:58.040
Prove that I was right.

770
01:05:58.694 --> 01:06:00.020
That we can be reborn.

771
01:06:00.189 --> 01:06:01.940
That we can
defeat death.

772
01:06:05.510 --> 01:06:09.660
But in the end. you turned out to be
just as much of a failure as the rest of them.

773
01:06:17.790 --> 01:06:19.760
Your grandfather
is a murderer. James.

774
01:06:19.865 --> 01:06:22.200
What can we do
when faced with a murderer?

775
01:06:22.804 --> 01:06:24.220
Are you absolutely sure?

776
01:06:24.249 --> 01:06:25.249
Yes.

777
01:06:25.535 --> 01:06:27.215
We can't just
wait.

778
01:06:27.415 --> 01:06:29.040
He doesn't deserve to die. okay?

779
01:06:30.260 --> 01:06:32.400
James... maybe it's better this way.

780
01:06:32.560 --> 01:06:33.640
I agree. Dudley is right.

781
01:06:33.940 --> 01:06:35.640
He did it to protect me!

782
01:06:35.894 --> 01:06:38.020
I'm not taking part in this.

783
01:06:38.720 --> 01:06:39.720
Whatever you want!

784
01:06:40.080 --> 01:06:41.080
Then stay here!

785
01:06:55.434 --> 01:06:57.010
That's strange...

786
01:06:58.490 --> 01:07:01.110
We both wanted to become
just like each other.

787
01:07:02.894 --> 01:07:04.490
Who am I descended from?

788
01:07:06.350 --> 01:07:07.590
From a little boy.

789
01:07:07.970 --> 01:07:09.330
A good friend of James's.

790
01:07:10.315 --> 01:07:11.315
Zack?

791
01:07:12.810 --> 01:07:14.330
So I came from...

792
01:07:15.210 --> 01:07:16.210
Zack?

793
01:07:16.629 --> 01:07:17.670
What on earth?

794
01:07:21.800 --> 01:07:24.172
I was hoping that
Zack's friendship with James.

795
01:07:24.372 --> 01:07:26.800
would prove that death
is not the end.

796
01:07:28.800 --> 01:07:29.260
That's enough.

797
01:07:29.480 --> 01:07:30.960
This is going from
bad to worse.

798
01:07:31.280 --> 01:07:32.080
I'm going to the police.

799
01:07:32.114 --> 01:07:34.420
Your grandpa is a monster.

800
01:07:35.100 --> 01:07:37.300
But I don't want to die.

801
01:07:38.750 --> 01:07:40.880
Your death is the
best thing that could happen to James

802
01:07:42.880 --> 01:07:43.880
No!

803
01:07:48.824 --> 01:07:49.850
You damn kid!

804
01:07:50.289 --> 01:07:51.910
I don't have time for you right now.

805
01:07:52.310 --> 01:07:53.930
We have to save him.

806
01:07:53.931 --> 01:07:54.931
Hurry up.

807
01:08:04.660 --> 01:08:05.660
Look here.

808
01:08:06.620 --> 01:08:07.620
James!

809
01:08:07.880 --> 01:08:08.100
One!

810
01:08:08.420 --> 01:08:09.540
My dad has gone crazy!

811
01:08:11.580 --> 01:08:11.960
I know.

812
01:08:12.380 --> 01:08:13.660
I don't want you to die.

813
01:08:13.920 --> 01:08:14.920
You're in danger.

814
01:08:17.380 --> 01:08:17.620
James!

815
01:08:17.979 --> 01:08:18.979
One!

816
01:08:30.638 --> 01:08:32.939
Stop! No!

817
01:08:40.109 --> 01:08:42.189
I know a place where we can hide.

818
01:08:42.689 --> 01:08:43.229
No!

819
01:08:43.430 --> 01:08:43.990
Come on!

820
01:08:44.149 --> 01:08:44.750
We have to go!

821
01:08:44.751 --> 01:08:45.609
James!

822
01:08:45.770 --> 01:08:47.490
They must die!

823
01:08:47.609 --> 01:08:48.609
Wait for me!

824
01:09:38.300 --> 01:09:40.640
And I'll bring Mia back. too.

825
01:09:41.540 --> 01:09:43.899
James... I did all of this for you.

826
01:09:44.279 --> 01:09:44.779
No.

827
01:09:44.780 --> 01:09:45.399
You didn't do it for me.

828
01:09:45.600 --> 01:09:46.319
No.

829
01:09:46.620 --> 01:09:48.100
That's what you wanted.

830
01:09:48.840 --> 01:09:52.160
Did you think no one would
ever find out the truth?

831
01:10:55.155 --> 01:10:56.420
Come on.

832
01:10:57.795 --> 01:10:59.260
Come on.

833
01:11:01.060 --> 01:11:01.720
Come on.

834
01:11:01.840 --> 01:11:03.220
Come on. boys and girls.

835
01:11:09.900 --> 01:11:12.260
I am on the verge of a
great discovery.

836
01:11:13.060 --> 01:11:14.740
Something greater than all of us.

837
01:11:19.580 --> 01:11:20.620
No... I can't.

838
01:11:24.390 --> 01:11:26.650
Dr. Gallow showed me
how to bring you back.

839
01:12:14.820 --> 01:12:15.420
No!

840
01:12:15.421 --> 01:12:16.740
You ruined everything!

841
01:12:59.630 --> 01:13:00.630
What the hell?

842
01:13:02.690 --> 01:13:04.310
You forget who you are.

843
01:13:04.770 --> 01:13:05.470
I created you.

844
01:13:05.471 --> 01:13:07.550
I'm not your puppet anymore.

845
01:13:07.670 --> 01:13:08.670
You are.

846
01:13:08.890 --> 01:13:10.750
Without me. you're
just a piece of wood.

847
01:13:11.230 --> 01:13:13.010
No. I'm more than that.

848
01:13:13.390 --> 01:13:17.410
A puppet needs a master.
and only I can make you real.

849
01:13:17.690 --> 01:13:19.030
Let me make you just like James.

850
01:13:19.031 --> 01:13:21.290
I don't want
to be like James anymore.

851
01:13:21.870 --> 01:13:23.450
I just want to be myself.

852
01:13:24.210 --> 01:13:26.170
You'll always feel empty inside.

853
01:13:27.090 --> 01:13:27.810
Incomplete.

854
01:13:28.110 --> 01:13:29.350
Broken.

855
01:13:30.010 --> 01:13:31.010
Maybe...

856
01:13:31.230 --> 01:13:33.610
But you can't
control me anymore.

857
01:13:35.050 --> 01:13:36.590
I gave you life.

858
01:13:36.790 --> 01:13:39.170
I'm not just
your father. Pinocchio.

859
01:13:39.390 --> 01:13:40.630
I am your god.

860
01:13:40.990 --> 01:13:44.150
And your god just
killed a god.

861
01:13:44.670 --> 01:13:45.670
Go fuck yourself.

862
01:13:47.470 --> 01:13:48.470
Goodbye.

863
01:13:49.880 --> 01:13:50.880
Oh God...

864
01:14:49.540 --> 01:14:50.540
James?

865
01:14:52.425 --> 01:14:54.600
Are we still friends?

866
01:15:00.025 --> 01:15:02.240
Am I... bad?

867
01:15:04.660 --> 01:15:06.280
You were just confused.

868
01:15:07.370 --> 01:15:09.500
Just... don't do that again. okay?

869
01:15:10.320 --> 01:15:12.500
I'm such an idiot...

870
01:15:14.420 --> 01:15:17.320
Yeah... after all. we all make mistakes.

871
01:15:17.525 --> 01:15:19.300
Except for my dentist.

872
01:15:21.120 --> 01:15:22.420
I'll need a new one.

873
01:15:24.180 --> 01:15:25.740
I'll find you someone else.

874
01:15:29.460 --> 01:15:32.600
You won't tell
anyone about me. will you?

875
01:15:36.940 --> 01:15:37.940
And you won't lie.

876
01:15:38.840 --> 01:15:39.200
Great.

877
01:15:39.495 --> 01:15:40.495
Me neither.

878
01:15:42.927 --> 01:15:43.459
Me?

879
01:15:44.920 --> 01:15:45.920
Let's go.

880
01:15:46.060 --> 01:15:47.060
We left.

881
01:15:50.570 --> 01:15:51.910
I'll beat you to it.

882
01:15:58.180 --> 01:15:59.180
Goodbye. Father.

883
01:16:01.560 --> 01:16:03.740
You created me.
but you don't control me anymore.

884
01:16:04.720 --> 01:16:05.720
James is my friend.

885
01:16:10.540 --> 01:16:11.540
No!

886
01:16:15.240 --> 01:16:17.080
Don't kill me!

887
01:16:18.980 --> 01:16:22.280
I didn't want to kill
all of them.

888
01:16:22.304 --> 01:16:49.204
Dialogue Translation &
Timing: Sparta
